the Mexican military hunts for Joaquin  Guzman otherwise known as El Chapo just  one of the dramatic videos shown to a  court during his trial in Brooklyn New  York in this instance they were too late  the drug kingpin escaped through a  tunnel hidden beneath the hydraulic  baths but now two years after he was  extradited to the United States  prosecutors have got their man el chapo  found guilty of drug trafficking and  money laundering attended daily by his  wife Emma El Chapo's trial has often  felt more like a script from a Hollywood  film it provided an extraordinary  glimpse into the brutal and lucrative  world of Mexico's Sinaloa cartel and how  El Chapo became its mastermind moving  thousands of kilos of illegal drugs into  the u.s. across its southern border the  court heard how El Chapo was a man who  liked to enjoy his vast wealth carrying  a diamond-encrusted handgun and using a  gold-plated  ak-47 even installing a private Zoo at  one of his properties but he was also  powerful and ruthless the court watching  a video of him interrogating a man tied  to a post and listening to stories about  purpose-built execution chambers and  obscene violence  one witness even alleged that he bribed  Mexico's former president Nieto an  accusation mr. Nieto dismissed as false  the jury wasn't convinced by El Chapo's  lawyers who spent just 30 minutes  presenting their clients defense arguing  that he was simply a scapegoat and  acting on the orders of someone else  instead they found him guilty of all 10  counts and now he faces life in prison  where he will be held under the tightest  security El Chapo has escaped prison in  Mexico twice before once in a laundry  cart and wants through a tunnel on a  motorbike it's why he's been transported  to and from his trial in a convoy of  armored vehicles the Department of  Justice taking no chances with their big  prize one of the most infamous drug  traffickers in the world now behind bars  Hannah Thomas Peter Sky News at fe